warning[pointer_lifetime]: `p` refers to an element in `t` whose identity is invalidated on every path to this use
   --> tests/lint/pointer_lifetime/movement/containers-bad.jai:15:10
    |
 13 |     p := H.table_find_pointer(*t, 7);
    |          --------------------------- pointer derived here
 14 |     H.table_remove(*t, 7);
    |     --------------------- `t` element moved or removed here
 15 |     sink(p);
    |          ^ pointer used here after its element was moved or removed
    |
   ::: [repo]/stdlib/internal/collections/hash-table.jai:351:17
    |
351 | table_remove :: (table: *Table, key: table.Key_Type) -> (success: bool, value: table.Value_Type) {
    |                 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- invalidation inferred through this call
    |
    = help: take the pointer again after the operation, or keep a stable key instead

